    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, the customer needs to make a purchase and then connect to the website."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly starts the process (init) and explicitly defines the first combined action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, they should search for an item."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the second sequential step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "guard:b1->n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If they choose to \"Add item to cart\", they can proceed to checkout. However, if they select \"Continue Shopping\", they should continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The XOR branch and its two outgoing guards faithfully capture the exclusive choice between the two stated options."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once they proceed to checkout, they need to enter their address, shipping method, and payment information."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the transition to checkout and the three required data-entry tasks."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "At the same time, they should also authorize the credit card and check the inventory levels."
      ],
      "justification": "The AND branch captures the 'at the same time' concurrency cue, while the action captures the two parallel tasks."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n10",
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the credit card is approved and there is inventory in stock, they can continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The guard and the redundant action step both faithfully restate the positive approval/in-stock condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "if the credit card is denied or there is no inventory in stock"
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the negative denial/out-of-stock condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the transaction will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Both action nodes and the terminal structural nodes cover the repeated instruction to end the transaction upon failure."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "the transaction will end"
      ],
      "justification": "Both action nodes and the terminal structural nodes cover the repeated instruction to end the transaction upon failure."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In either case, the order confirmation number should be displayed, followed by the final order being shown to the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "'In either case' signals path convergence, followed by the two sequential display actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, the order should be confirmed and a confirmation notice should be emailed to the customer."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the two post-convergence administrative actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the order entry is complete, the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the completion checkpoint and the explicit process termination."
    }
